---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Stadium Ceiling Maintenance & Construction — ARCLIFT"
  description="Project screening for crawler platforms used in stadium acoustic-panel, lighting and overhead service work, with bearing, access, exclusion-zone and rescue checks."
  transparentNav={false}
>

  <section class="hero-banner" style="--banner-image:url('/images/banners/stadium.webp');--banner-position:center 58%;">
    <div class="overline">Stadium & Arena</div>
    <h1>STADIUM CEILING SOLUTIONS</h1>
    <p>Large-span steel structures, acoustic panel installation, rigging access, and lighting maintenance.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
      <h2 style="font-size:28px;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:20px;">Stadium Project Screening</h2>
      <p style="font-size:16px;color:#475569;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">Stadium work may involve acoustic panels, lighting grids, services and periodic inspection across a large plan area. The available route, field or concourse bearing, roof geometry, event calendar and safe recovery method determine whether a large-deck crawler is practical.</p>
      <p style="font-size:16px;color:#475569;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">ARC-F pages describe reference concepts rather than a guaranteed one-machine solution. A project study must confirm reachable work zones, deck load, stabilizing method, floor protection, exclusion zones and local work-at-height requirements.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec--gray">
    <div class="sec__header reveal">
      <div class="sec__overline">Recommended Models</div>
      <h2 class="sec__title">FOR STADIUM WORK</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px;max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;">
      <div style="padding:32px;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;border:1px solid #f1f5f9;">
        <h3 style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:12px;">ARC-F35 — Reference High-Reach Concept</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:#64748b;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:20px;">For early feasibility checks at taller work zones. Model-specific proof of reach, platform geometry, load chart and transport data is required.</p>
        <a href="/products/arc-f35-crawler-ceiling-platform/" class="btn btn--outline-blue">View Model →</a>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:32px;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;border:1px solid #f1f5f9;">
        <h3 style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:12px;">ARC-F31 — High-Reach</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:#64748b;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:20px;">A second reference size for projects where access and bearing constraints rule out the largest concept. Compare approved drawings, not model names alone.</p>
        <a href="/products/arc-f31-crawler-ceiling-platform/" class="btn btn--outline-blue">View Model →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <h2>PLANNING STADIUM CEILING WORK?</h2>
    <p>Tell us your roof height and access constraints — we'll spec the right ARC configuration.</p>
    <a href="/contact/" class="btn--white">Get a Project Assessment →</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
